// Data: values, typed strings, configuration, types and enums, and encodings.
include = [
  "./values.heron",
  "./typed_strings.heron",
  "./configuration.heron.md",
  "./types.heron",
  "./encodings.heron.md",
]

@lens(user, developer)
| Data written in Heron: values and their types, the strings a type parses, configuration, types and enums, and how values encode. One set of declarations describes data, APIs and configuration, so a spec works as an IDL and a config format at once. Values use the [core format](#language.core_format.values)'s literals; APIs and their transports are under [APIs](#language.apis).
